            <ArticleTitle>[Significance of the ear in the determination of age].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>172-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The morphology of human ear conch is said to be rather individual, but a perfect person-identification by this mean is not possible. It is demonstrated by photographs-made in a 15 years' interval-that ear conch and auricular area can be typically marked by proceeding age and specific diseases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
